# Fallback on-screen keyboard policy (task 014 P2b; report 042: Settings > System > On-screen keyboard is Auto / On, Off
# is gone), end to end with APPLAUNCH_OSK=auto (the normal rule) and the harness' presence fixture ("keyboards N"): a
# stored Off (osk_mode 1, an earlier version's) reads as Auto, so the Keyboard test field gets the keyboard; a physical
# keyboard appears: it goes within the policy poll (250 ms); On through the choice list: the keyboard shows even with
# the physical keyboard (vkb=force). Review only, no golden.
title on-screen keyboard policy
review
sizes 640x480 800x480
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 1
env APPLAUNCH_OSK auto
config osk_mode 1
keyboards 0
apps Settings Store CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
expect_mode 0
launch Settings
# System (the last section); from its end: Shutdown, Reboot, Keyboard test, On-screen keyboard
key UP
key ENTER
key UP
key UP
key UP
key ENTER
expect_osk shown
expect_vkb auto
expect_hand 0
shot osk_policy_old_off
keyboards 1
wait 400
expect_osk hidden
shot osk_policy_keyboard_appeared
# Esc stops editing, Esc again leaves the form; the choice list: Auto is checked, Down then Enter picks On
key ESC
key ESC
key UP
key ENTER
wait 300
shot osk_policy_choice
key DOWN
key ENTER
expect_mode 2
key DOWN
key ENTER
wait 400
expect_osk shown
expect_vkb force
shot osk_policy_on
